      "title": {
        "en": "Skilled and empathetic veterinary team"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Clients consistently praise veterinarians including Dr. Robins, Dr. Ortega, Dr. Quesada, and Dr. Diaz-Cruz for their attentive care, warm energy, and clinical dedication. Pet owners appreciate thorough examinations and supportive staff, although a few reviewers expressed dissatisfaction with office management."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "results",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 18,
      "title": {
        "en": "Trusted specialty care and eye treatment"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Pet owners frequently highlight excellent treatment outcomes, particularly praising board-certified veterinary ophthalmologist Dr. Karpinski for managing complex vision and eye conditions. Reviewers note accurate diagnoses and noticeable improvements in their pets' recovery and comfort."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "animals",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 15,
      "title": {
        "en": "Gentle handling for sensitive pets"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Reviewers appreciate the team's gentle, patient demeanor with dogs and cats, from playful puppies to aging senior animals with chronic ailments. Owners note that staff take time to soothe nervous pets during physical exams and diagnostic tests, ensuring animals feel secure throughout visits."
      }
    }
  ],
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": {
        "en": "Does Pinecrest Veterinary Hospital offer veterinary ophthalmology?"
      },
      "a": {
        "en": "Yes, the hospital features specialized eye care led by Dr. Karpinski, a board-certified veterinary ophthalmologist."
      },
      "basis": "both"
    },
    {
